'<!-- Section properties of a solid circle: area, $I_x = I_y = \pi d^4 / 64$, section modulus and radius of gyration. -->
"Geometrical Properties of Circle
'<div style="max-width:120mm"><img style="height:135pt;" alt="circle.png" class="side" src="../../Images/mechanics/sections/circle.png"></div>
'Diameter
d = ? {1}'m
'Area
A = π*d^2/4'm<sup>2</sup>
'Centroid
'<p><i>z</i><sub>c</sub> ='y_c = d/2'm</p>
'Perimeter
P = π*d'm
'Second moments of area
'<p><i>I</i><sub>z</sub> ='I_y = π*d^4/64'm<sup>4</sup></p>
'Polar moment of area
I_x = 2*I_y'm<sup>4</sup>
'Radii of gyration
'<p><i>r</i><sub>z</sub> ='r_y = sqrt(I_y/A)'m</p>
r_x = sqr(I_x/A)'m
'Torsional constant
I_t = π*d^4/32'm<sup>4</sup>
'Torsional section modulus
W_t = 2*I_t/d'm<sup>3</sup>
